---
const ages = [
  { name:"Satya", years:"1,728,000", share:4, href:"/atlas/satya-yuga" },
  { name:"Treta", years:"1,296,000", share:3, href:"/atlas/treta-yuga" },
  { name:"Dvapara", years:"864,000", share:2, href:"/atlas/dvapara-yuga" },
  { name:"Kali", years:"432,000", share:1, href:"/atlas/kali-yuga" },
];
---
<figure class="yuga-scale surface">
  <figcaption>One Maha Yuga: four ages, 4.32 million human years</figcaption>
  <div class="scale-bar" aria-hidden="true">{ages.map(age => <span style={`flex:${age.share}`} class:list={{current:age.name === "Kali"}}>{age.share}</span>)}</div>
  <ol>{ages.map(age => <li><a href={age.href} aria-current={age.name === "Kali" ? "page" : undefined}><strong>{age.name}{age.name === "Kali" && " · Present age"}</strong><span>{age.years} years</span></a></li>)}</ol>
  <p>The traditional duration ratio is 4 : 3 : 2 : 1, including each age's transitions. Source: Vishnu Purana I.3.</p>
</figure>
<style>
  figure { margin:1.5rem 0; padding:1.2rem; box-shadow:none; }
  figcaption { color:var(--ink); font-weight:700; }
  .scale-bar { display:flex; gap:4px; margin:1rem 0; }
  .scale-bar span { padding:.4rem; text-align:center; color:var(--ink); background:var(--surface-muted); border:1px solid var(--border); }
  .scale-bar .current { border:2px solid var(--copper); }
  ol { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:.6rem; list-style:none; padding:0; }
  a { display:grid; min-height:44px; padding:.5rem; border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:.5rem; }
  a[aria-current] { border-color:var(--copper); }
  a span, p { color:var(--ink-muted); font-size:.85rem; }
  p { margin-bottom:0; }
</style>
